<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Tell</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>tell &lt;character&gt; &lt;words&gt;
tell group &lt;words&gt;
<a cmd='#'>tell</a>
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>tell asta Meet me at the temple!
</pre>
<p>You may speak to a player who is anywhere in the game with the tell command. 
No other player will hear it. tell group &lt;words&gt; tells everyone in your group.
</p><p><a cmd='#'>tell</a> alone shows your last 20 tells; <a cmd='#'>clear tell</a> empties that list. To answer 
the last one who told you something, use <a cmd='#'>Help Respond</a>.
</p><p>A player who doesn't want to hear tells can turn them off with <a cmd='#'>change tell</a>, 
and on again the same way; they can also ignore a single player (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Ignore</a>). Beware that gods can see the messages you send and receive, 
though it is considered rude to look.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Respond</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ignore</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Say</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Whisper</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ask</a>
</pre>




</div>